From Superman's creators, Jerry Siegel and Joe Shuster (originally Segalovich and Shusterowich), to Batman's Bill Finger and Bob Kane (Kahn), to Marvel's Jack Kirby (Kurtzberg) and Stan Lee (Lieber), American superheroes emerged from the pens and inks of Jewish artists who transformed comics into both mass entertainment and serious literature. In this course, we will examine significant comics and graphic novels from the 1930s to the present to explore how Jewish identity and the diaspora experience shape superhero storytelling. Drawing on frameworks from cultural studies, rabbinic tradition, media studies, and postcolonial theory, we will explore themes of assimilation, otherness, and moral responsibility. No prior knowledge of comics or Jewish studies required. Restricted to first-year students. Not eligible for CR/NCR option.", "title": "Jews, Superheroes, and Other Curiosities", "levelOfInstruction": null, "prerequisitesText": "", "corequisitesText": "", "exclusionsText": "", "recommendedPreparation": "", "note": null, "division": "Arts and Science, Faculty of", "breadthRequirements": ["Creative and Cultural Representations (1)"], "distributionRequirements": ["Humanities"], "publicationSections": ["First-Year Foundations", "Centre for Jewish Studies"], "cmPublicationSections": [{"section": "First-Year Foundations", "subSections": null}, {"section": "Centre for Jewish Studies", "subSections": null}]}, "created": "2026-04-21@23:19:36.416", "modified": null, "lastSaved": 0, "primaryTeachMethod": "LEC", "faculty": {"code": "ARTSC", "name": "Faculty of Arts and Science"}, "coSec": {"code": "", "name": null}, "department": {"code": "JSP", "name": "Jewish Studies"}, "title": null, "maxCredit": 0.5, "minCredit": 0.5, "breadths": [{"org": {"code": "ARTSC", "name": "Faculty of Arts and Science"}, "breadthTypes": [{"kind": "BREADTH", "type": "Creative Cultural", "description": "BR=1 Creative and Cultural Representation", "code": "BR=1"}]}], "notes": [{"name": "Course Note", "type": "COURSE", "content": "<p><strong>Timetable Instructions</strong></p><p>This is a <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://www.artsci.utoronto.ca/future/academic-opportunities/first-year-opportunities/first-year-foundations-seminars\">First Year Seminar</a> course. We encourage all first year students to enrol in this course! No prior knowledge is necessary.&nbsp;</p>"}], "cancelInd": "", "subscriptionTtb": false, "subscriptionOpenData": false, "tb1Active": false, "tb2Active": false, "fullyOnline": false, "primaryFull": false, "primaryWaitlistable": false}, {"id": "69dd3ea4830c3634bbb69966", "name": "Introduction to Jewish Thought", "ucName": null, "code": "CJS200H1", "sectionCode": "S", "campus": "St. George", "sessions": ["20271"], "sections": [{"name": "LEC0101", "type": "Lecture", "teachMethod": "LEC", "sectionNumber": "0101", "meetingTimes": null, "firstMeeting": null, "instructors": null, "currentEnrolment": null, "maxEnrolment": null, "subTitle": null, "cancelInd": null, "waitlistInd": null, "deliveryModes": [], "currentWaitlist": null, "enrolmentInd": null, "tbaInd": null, "openLimitInd": null, "notes": [{"name": "Section Note", "type": "SECTION", "content": ""}], "enrolmentControls": null, "linkedMeetingSections": null}], "duration": null, "cmCourseInfo": {"description": "A balanced presentation of the multifaceted approach to the discipline by treating Jewish religion and thought. The course introduces students not only to a chronological and thematic overview of the subject, but also to different methodological approaches.", "title": "Introduction to Jewish Thought", "levelOfInstruction": "undergraduate", "prerequisitesText": "", "corequisitesText": "", "exclusionsText": "", "recommendedPreparation": "", "note": null, "division": "Arts and Science, Faculty of", "breadthRequirements": ["Thought, Belief and Behaviour (2)"], "distributionRequirements": ["Humanities"], "publicationSections": ["Centre for Jewish Studies"], "cmPublicationSe